<title>TURKEY: Turkey raises local sugar prices by 18 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkey raises local sugar prices by 18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's state sugar refineries Turkseker raised local wholesale sugar prices by 18 percent with immediate effect, officials said.</p>
<p>They said the price of a 50-kilo sack would rise to 3,537,000 lira from 2,997,000 for white sugar. Its per kilo price was raised to 70,740 lira from 58,190.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom +90-312-4462940</p>
